  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: town in E Sicily. In 263 BC Appius Claudius Caudex unsuccessfully laid siege to Echetla. While the <em>Barrington Atlas</em> does not offer a precise location, some scholars (viz. G. Falco in <em>New Pauly</em>) associate the ancient site with the ruins on the hill of Occhiol\u00e0 near Grammichele. The remains of a sanctuary dedicated to Demeter have been excavated there.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient settlement, attested by literary or documentary sources, whose precise location cannot be determined today",
